// Ch4 C4-11 "Cutscene: the Seventh Terrace" (docs/kb/story/beats/act1_ch04.md). 07:30, mid-strait. A
// lookout's call. F05 (50 mm, from the ferry's rail): a ship off the bow under full sail, red-and-black
// lacquer, copper sheathing, running before the wind with nobody at the helm, the wheel turning by
// itself. Held motes (glimmer_held, faint in daylight) hang in her rigging like spray that won't fall.
// Rhen knows her: Sadi Moru's coaster from Oruvel's outer mooring, which ran for open water when the
// gulls cried (act1_ch01.md C1-09, C1-12). The first proof since the beach that Oruvel was real and
// that it's gone.
// Sea-law (bible §5.1): no hull drowned in a Rising is passed without someone bringing its name-board
// home. Imbe will lie alongside, an oar's length off, with fenders and boathooks, because you never
// lash a living hull to a drowned one, and he won't send his crew aboard (ferrymen with families; the
// rigging is moving wrong). Rhen goes; Asha won't let him go alone; Toma goes because she goes;
// Ysolde goes because someone should say the Canticle over a drowned hull correctly.
// D01: Rhen jumping the gap to her chain-plates.
// ADR 0017 (d): the ferry is never attacked, and nothing from the derelict comes aboard her.
// Music: brightwater_crossing -> silence. The chapter flow sets ch04_boarded_derelict.
title: ch04_seventh_terrace
location: ch04/brightwater_ferry
---
@letterbox on
@sfx lookout_call
Ferrymaster [surprised]: Sail! Sail off the bow, and she's not answering! #line:ch04_terrace_001
@camera F05
@vfx glimmer_held at=derelict_rigging count=12 rate=hang
@sfx derelict_wheel_turning
@music silence fade=3.0
@wait 2.5
Rhen [surprised]: That's the Seventh Terrace. #line:ch04_terrace_002
Rhen [grief]: She was tied up at Oruvel three days ago. Her skipper paid me short. #line:ch04_terrace_003
@wait 1.5
Ferrymaster [neutral]: Then she drowned in the Rising, and she's still sailing. #line:ch04_terrace_004
Ferrymaster [determined]: Sea-law. You don't pass a drowned hull without bringing her name-board home. #line:ch04_terrace_005
Ferrymaster [neutral]: I'll lie alongside her, an oar's length off. Fenders and boathooks. #line:ch04_terrace_006
Ferrymaster [worried]: You never lash a living hull to a drowned one. And my crew stays aboard. #line:ch04_terrace_007
Ferrymaster [worried]: Look at her rigging. It's moving wrong. #line:ch04_terrace_008
Rhen [determined]: I'm a diver. I've been on more drowned hulls than anyone on this deck. I'll go. #line:ch04_terrace_009
Asha [determined]: You're my guardian. Guardians walk behind. So I'll go first. #line:ch04_terrace_010
Toma [exhausted]: Then I am going. #line:ch04_terrace_011
Ysolde [neutral]: Someone should say the Canticle over her correctly. I am the only one aboard who may. #line:ch04_terrace_012
@camera D01
@anim rhen jump_gap
@sfx gangplank
@wait 1.5
@letterbox off
===
